[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) is marked known: one issue, one fix queued. Its reports show three
problems. One fix closes one of them. The other two had no ticket, so this page files one each.

<Callout kind="warn">
The queued parser fix does not close #4471. The form hint and the one-day moves stay broken after it ships.
</Callout>

## The split

<ProblemTable ticket={4471} {tickets} />

Each report is placed by its tenant and channel (`causes.ts`), except the reports the desk
already read as a one-day move (`desk-notes.json`). Those are kept apart. Reports that came twice
in the export are counted once.

## The three problems

### `parser`: the shared parser reads dates month first

It covers <ProblemCount ticket={4471} problem="parser" /> reports. Every tenant on file writes the day first.
The shared parser reads month first, so a booking for 7 April goes out for 4 July. This is the
fix that is already queued, and it closes this row only.

### `hint`: booking-v3 prints `MM/DD/YYYY` and reads day first

It covers <ProblemCount ticket={4471} problem="hint" /> reports. All of them came through the booking form, at the
tenants that run booking-v3. The form tells people to type the month first, then reads what they
typed the tenant's way, day first. The parser fix does not touch this form. The hint or the
reading must change.

### `one-day`: the date moves by one day

It covers <ProblemCount ticket={4471} problem="one-day" /> reports. The date is not swapped. It moves by a
day: "Client in Lisbon got Tuesday. Client in Toronto got Monday. Same meeting." That points at
time zones, not date order. The desk already noted these reports, then filed them under `parser`
by tenant. The parser fix will not move them back.

## How #4471 looked

The table on the incident page puts every report under one of two causes:

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

## Lessons

- Merging on subject alone ([decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject)) put three problems behind one subject family. A count tells you how loud a ticket is, not how many bugs it holds.
- Read the reports the desk itself marked as odd before you call a ticket known.

